---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  Alerts show a short, contextual message inside the page, with a leading icon and a clear label. For a
  transient message use <a href='/components/snackbar'><code>wc-snackbar</code></a>, or
  <a href='/components/notification-manager'><code>wc-notification-manager</code></a> for a queue of them.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-alert
    description='These color roles were chosen to create design coherence and familiarity.'>
  </wc-alert>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>Use slots to customize icon, label, and content.</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-alert>
    <wc-icon slot='icon' name='campaign'></wc-icon>
    <span slot='label'>Announcement:</span>
    Scheduled maintenance starts at 12:00 UTC.
  </wc-alert>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Actions and closing</h3>

<p>
  Put buttons in the <code>action</code> slot. <code>dismissible</code> adds a close button: pressing it
  fires a cancelable <code>close</code> event with <code>detail.reason</code> <code>'action'</code>, then
  the alert hides itself (sets <code>hidden</code>). Call <code>preventDefault()</code> on the event to keep
  it, for example to remove it from your own state instead.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-alert id='trial-alert' intent='warning' dismissible description='Your trial ends in 3 days.'>
    <wc-button slot='action' variant='text' size='sm'>Upgrade</wc-button>
  </wc-alert>

  <p id='alert-log' class='text-body'> </p>

  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#trial-alert').addEventListener('close', event => {
      document.querySelector('#alert-log').textContent = `Alert closed (${event.detail.reason})`;
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Announcing</h3>

<p>
  An alert is not a live region by default, so an alert that is there when the page loads is read in the
  normal order instead of being announced. For an alert you add or change while the page is in use, set
  <code>live='polite'</code> (<code>role="status"</code>) or, for urgent messages only,
  <code>live='assertive'</code> (<code>role="alert"</code>).
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-alert live='polite' intent='success' description='Your changes were saved.'></wc-alert>
</DemoComponentCard>
